    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0223" n="211" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg211"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50 UNRRA/11–2744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Representative on
                        the Advisory Council for Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-02T19:00:00-04:00">December 2, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>444. Department somewhat concerned over statement made by Jackson (Caserta No.
                    1515, November 27—UNRRA from Jackson No. 95<anchor n="32a" xml:id="d221-f1"/>)
                    that continuance of use of Swedish ships is not related to continuing <pb
                        facs="0224" n="212" xml:id="pg212"/> operations of Swedish-Swiss Commission.
                    As stated in our No. 33 to Athens<anchor n="33" xml:id="d221-f2"/> the question
                    of Swedish ships is now under discussion with Swedish Government and it appears
                    that continuance of Swedish-Swiss Commission at least in &amp; nominal capacity
                    may be necessary in order to assure continued use of the ships. You will be
                    advised of any further developments.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Athens.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
